## Phase 6 — maintenance notes (read, don't execute)

- For a `-git` package, AUR helpers re-run `pkgver()` on update checks — you don't bump `pkgver` for new commits. Bump `pkgrel` (reset to 1 only on a `pkgver` change) only when you change the PKGBUILD itself without an upstream commit.
- After any PKGBUILD change: regenerate `.SRCINFO` before committing — a stale `.SRCINFO` is one of the most common AUR flagging reasons.
- If you ever wire more `config.yaml` tunables (NG4), keep `backup=("usr/share/swipetype/config.yaml")` — pacman preserves a user's edited config across updates (`.pacnew`). Remember the packaged `config.yaml` is root-owned; per-user runtime state (like overlay layout) belongs under `~/.local/state/swipetype/`, not in that file.
- 🆕 **Restyling the overlay** = edit `overlay-app/ui/style.css` (and constants at the top of `overlay.js`), preview with `index.html?demo`, commit. No PKGBUILD change is needed unless you add new files (they're picked up by the `cp -r` of `ui/`) or new dependencies.
- 🆕 If a future WebKitGTK or gtk4-layer-shell update breaks transparency or layering, re-run the Stage 2a spike (`scratch/spike_webkit.py`) first — it isolates platform issues from your code.
- 🆕 If you later want GNOME/KDE support (NG1), the webview UI is reusable as-is; only the host window (layer-shell → a regular always-on-top transparent window or a shell-extension approach) would need a second backend.